nised for all $n\\ge 5$. This proves a strengthening of two conjectures of Dey.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUmesh Shankar - Publications (https://sites.google.com/view/umeshshankar/publications)\nciteturn8search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Enumerative Combinatorics and Applications, Vol 4, Article #S2R3, 2024. available at arXiv:2211.15277 [math.CO] ... Synchronicity of descent and excedance enumerators in the alternating subgroup ... Niranjan Balachandran, Ankita Dargad, Urban Larsson, Neeldhara Misra, Umesh Shankar\n\nPDF\n\nSynchronicity of descent and excedance enumerators in the alternating subgroup\n\nUmesh Shankar\n\nDiscrete Math. 348, No. 8, Article ID 114521, 9 p (2025), available at arXiv:2404.01783 [math.CO]\n\nPDF\n\nA descent-excedance correspondence in colored permutation groups\n\nHiranya Kishore Dey , Umesh Shankar, Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian\n\nEnumer. Comb. Appl. 5, No. 3, Article ID S2R24, 11 p. (2025),  available at arXiv:2410.23206 [math.CO]\n\nPDF\n\nA combinatorial method for log-concavity of rows of triangular arrays\n\nUmesh Shankar\n\naccepted at Electronic Journal of Combinatorics, a vailable at  arXiv:2508.12467 [math.CO]\n\nPDF \n\n\nConference Publications\n\nFerry Cover with Connectivity Constraints\n\nNiranjan Balachandran, Ankita Dargad, Urban Larsson, Neeldhara Misra, Umesh Shankar\n\naccepted at FUN with Algorithms, 2026.\n\nPDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nElectronic Journal of Linear Algebra, ISSN 1081-3810 (https://orbi.umons.ac.be/bitstream/20.500.12907/54217/1/GLT%20SEQUENCES%20AND%20NORMAL%20MATRICES.pdf)\nciteturn8search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; GLT 6. ... The ﬁrst main result of this paper (Theorem 3.1) delivers a normal form for every GLT sequence.\nTheorem 3.1 (normal form for GLT sequences).\nThroughout this paper, we denote by On and In the n × n zero matrix and the n × n id